WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.986
In this video you will learn how to sign in to
OurWater, what to do if you forget your password,

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.338
and how to sign out safely.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.358
This is the sign-in page.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:15.510
You see it whenever you open OurWater and you
are not signed in.

00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:18.909
The language button is in the top corner.

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:22.053
Press it to see a list of popular languages.

00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:26.987
Below them, a longer menu holds more than
sixty languages.

00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:29.963
OurWater remembers the one you choose.

00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:36.423
Choose how to sign in: with your email address, or
with the username you picked when you joined.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.970
Press Username, and the box asks for that
instead.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.602
If your school or organisation made your
account, use Username.

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:48.289
Type your username.

00:00:48.409 --> 00:00:52.201
Small letters or capital letters, it does not
matter.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:54.889
Then your password.

00:00:55.009 --> 00:00:58.417
The dots hide it from anyone looking at your
screen.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.362
Not sure you typed it right?

00:01:01.482 --> 00:01:04.074
Press the eye to show your password.

00:01:04.194 --> 00:01:06.306
Press it again to hide it.

00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:08.989
Press Sign in.

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:12.901
If the details do not match, a red message
appears.

00:01:13.021 --> 00:01:15.469
Check each letter and try again.

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:20.171
Too many wrong tries in a row means a wait of
a few minutes.

00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:24.227
If you cannot remember, use Forgot password
instead.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.050
Now the right password, and Sign in.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.762
OurWater opens your home page.

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:33.834
The first time, this may take a moment.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.442
To sign out, press your round picture at the
bottom left.

00:01:38.562 --> 00:01:41.682
A menu opens, with Sign out in red.

00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:44.955
Press Sign out and you are back here.

00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:47.355
Your measurements stay saved.

00:01:47.475 --> 00:01:50.283
Always sign out on shared devices.

00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:52.989
New here?

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:55.245
Press Create a free account.

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:58.293
Another video in this series shows how.

00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:03.485
These two links open the Terms and Conditions
and the Privacy Policy.

00:02:03.605 --> 00:02:06.101
You can read them before you sign up.

00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:08.813
Forgot your password?

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:10.997
It happens to everyone.

00:02:11.117 --> 00:02:14.573
Press Forgot password, under the Sign in
button.

00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:20.159
Type the email address your account uses, and
press Send reset code.

00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:27.679
If your account has no email, ask your organisation's
administrator for new sign-in details instead.

00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:32.827
A six-digit code is sent to your email, and
this page opens.

00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:36.283
If it is late, check your junk or spam folder.

00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:38.989
Still nothing?

00:02:39.109 --> 00:02:41.077
Press Resend code.

00:02:41.197 --> 00:02:44.629
You can ask once a minute, a few times a day.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.114
Type the six numbers from your email.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.538
The code works for thirty minutes.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:57.182
Now a new password: at least eight characters,
with a capital letter, a small letter,

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:59.270
a number and a symbol.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.462
If it is too weak, the rule turns red.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:08.131
Type a stronger one that only you would know,
then press Update password.

00:03:08.251 --> 00:03:11.563
You return to sign in, with a green message.

00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:17.735
Sign in again: choose Email, then type your
address and your new password.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:23.182
The first time you sign in, OurWater asks you
to read two pages.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.302
It asks again whenever the Terms change.

00:03:27.117 --> 00:03:31.149
Two links open the Terms and Conditions and
the Privacy Policy.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:33.933
Please read both before you agree.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.766
This is the Terms page.

00:03:36.886 --> 00:03:43.558
Numbered sections explain what OurWater is for, how
accounts work, and how monitoring data is shared.

00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:46.687
This is the Privacy Policy.

00:03:46.807 --> 00:03:52.303
Its summary says what information we keep, and
that we do not sell personal information.

00:03:53.117 --> 00:03:57.389
Back on the page, notice that Accept and
continue is faded.

00:03:57.509 --> 00:04:00.605
It turns on only when you tick both boxes.

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:05.329
Tick that you agree, and that you are eighteen
or older.

00:04:05.449 --> 00:04:09.313
Younger people can join through a school or
organisation.

00:04:10.117 --> 00:04:11.989
Not ready?

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:15.589
Press Sign out instead, and nothing is saved.

00:04:16.417 --> 00:04:18.673
Press Accept and continue.

00:04:18.793 --> 00:04:22.993
You are in, and next time you will go straight
to your home page.

00:04:23.817 --> 00:04:28.545
That is how to sign in, reset a forgotten
password, and sign out.

00:04:28.665 --> 00:04:31.329
Thanks for helping look after our water.
